content:
{
  "summary": "Microsoft Defender on this computer is effectively not protecting it: real-time scanning is off, the entire C: drive is excluded from scanning, and tamper protection is off. Together these mean malware could arrive and run without being noticed, so restoring Defender's protection is the first thing to do. There is also one extra administrator account to confirm you recognize.",
  "groups": [
    {
      "priority": 1,
      "title": "Defender is switched off and told to ignore the whole C: drive",
      "finding_ids": [
        "DEF-REALTIME-OFF:6ed445bc",
        "DEF-EXCLUSION:c2d1c54c",
        "DEF-TAMPER-OFF:1a04a8d2"
      ],
      "explanation": "These three settings work together. Real-time protection is off, so Defender isn't checking files as they arrive. On top of that, all of C:\\ is on Defender's exclusion list. That is where Windows, your programs and your files normally live, so even a manual scan would skip almost everything. Tamper protection is also off, which means other programs are allowed to change Defender's settings like this. Defender's virus definitions are up to date (0 days old), but that doesn't help while it isn't scanning. This combination is sometimes the result of someone turning things off for troubleshooting and forgetting to turn them back on. It is also exactly what malware tries to do to hide. If you didn't make these changes yourself, treat it as a warning sign. The report shows the fix for each finding. Turning tamper protection back on helps keep the other settings from being changed again."
    },
    {
      "priority": 2,
      "title": "Confirm you recognize the extra administrator account",
      "finding_ids": [
        "ACCT-EXTRA-ADMIN:fde0b291"
      ],
      "explanation": "There is a local account, <computer>\\<account-2>, with full control of the computer. Having a separate administrator account is often good practice, so this may be completely normal if you or someone you trust created it. Because Defender's protection has been weakened, it's worth taking a moment to confirm you know what this account is. If you don't recognize it, the report shows how to deal with it."
    }
  ],
  "severity_notes": [
    {
      "finding_id": "DEF-TAMPER-OFF:1a04a8d2",
      "suggested_severity": "high",
      "reason": "On its own, medium is reasonable. Here, though, real-time protection is already off and the whole C: drive is excluded, which is the kind of change tamper protection exists to block. That makes it more serious in this context."
    }
  ]
}
